From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:48:45 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: hold the PMC performance floor while
 decoding

Linux decodes at about half the speed it could on the M4 Pro because
nothing raises the SoC rail while the decoder works; macOS votes a VMAX
floor for the decoder whenever frames are queued. Holding the SoC rail
at its performance level from the AP's PMC agent took H.264 1080p from
326 to 695 fps, AV1 4K from 198 to 420 and VP9 4K from 82 to 183 on a
J616s, every frame bit-exact against software decode.

A node can now list that floor as a second power domain, "perf", next
to the decoder's own. With more than one domain the core attaches none,
so attach them all with runtime PM device links: the floor is held
exactly while the decoder is runtime-active (frames in flight plus the
100 ms autosuspend delay) and released when it idles, rests or is
retired. The floor domain is shared and refcounted by genpd, so the
encoder's vote and this one combine. Nodes without it are unchanged.

The domain list is attached with runtime PM device links (the core
attaches no domain itself once there are several), and the links'
initial active references are settled before runtime PM is enabled, as
the encoder does, so the floor is not held from probe until the first
decode.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 5c6bfa057dc09bba4b6bb65423674405259e8673)
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd.h     |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c
index 986855879c..2ecae5ed58 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-drv.c
@@ -11,6 +11,8 @@
  * Copyright (C) 2011 Samsung Electronics Co., Ltd.
  */
 
+#include <linux/of.h>
+#include <linux/pm_domain.h>
 #include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
 #include <linux/iommu.h>
 #include <linux/reset.h>
@@ -854,6 +856,26 @@ static int avd_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	avd->rstc = devm_reset_control_get_exclusive(avd->dev, NULL);
 
+	/*
+	 * A node may list a second power domain, "perf": the PMC floor that
+	 * holds the SoC rail at its performance level while the decoder works
+	 * (decode runs at about half speed on the M4 Pro without it). With more
+	 * than one domain the core attaches none, so attach them all with
+	 * runtime PM device links: the floor is then held exactly while the
+	 * decoder is runtime-active (frames in flight plus the autosuspend
+	 * delay) and released when it idles, rests or is retired.
+	 */
+	if (of_count_phandle_with_args(pdev->dev.of_node, "power-domains",
+				       "#power-domain-cells") > 1) {
+		static const struct dev_pm_domain_attach_data pd_data = {
+			.pd_flags = PD_FLAG_DEV_LINK_ON,
+		};
+
+		ret = devm_pm_domain_attach_list(avd->dev, &pd_data, &avd->pd_list);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return dev_err_probe(avd->dev, ret, "failed to attach power domains\n");
+	}
+
 	avd->code = devm_platform_ioremap_resource_byname(pdev, "code");
 	if (IS_ERR(avd->code))
 		return PTR_ERR(avd->code);
@@ -923,6 +945,16 @@ static int avd_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The domain links were added active, but the decoder starts
+	 * suspended: settle that before enabling runtime PM, so the floor is
+	 * not held until the first decode has come and gone.
+	 */
+	if (avd->pd_list) {
+		ret = pm_runtime_set_suspended(avd->dev);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
 	pm_runtime_set_autosuspend_delay(avd->dev, 100);
 	pm_runtime_use_autosuspend(avd->dev);
 	pm_runtime_enable(avd->dev);
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd.h b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd.h
index fd77a0163e..f2921604e9 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd.h
@@ -217,6 +217,8 @@ struct avd_dev {
 
 	struct iommu_domain *domain;
 	struct iommu_domain *empty_domain;
+	/* Core and perf-floor domains when the node lists more than one. */
+	struct dev_pm_domain_list *pd_list;
 
 	struct mutex vdev_lock;
 
